      "message": "I think this should more be worded as, \"When this is called Skia will no longer try to fulfill any more BackendTextures.\" Because even in the current way you have it setup, it can easily outlive the SkImage. Like if you record a draw with that SkImage, then delete the SkImage, then snap a Recording. The fulfill won\u0027t be called until the snap is made.\n\nI wouldn\u0027t add this to the public comment here, but right now internally this is tied to the lifetime of the internal TextureProxy that gets made.",
